{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "a3f2c1d4-8b7e-4f9a-bc12-3e5d7a9f0123",
    "name": "Webbeet UX Audit Tool",
    "description": "# Webbeet UX Audit Tool API\n\nPublic-facing audit tool that scores a website across 6 categories: Performance, SEO, Trust, UX Signals, Mobile, and Accessibility.\n\n## Environments\n\nSwitch between environments using the environment selector:\n- **Local** - `http://localhost:3000` (dev server)\n- **Production** - Railway URL (set after Day 5 deploy)\n\n## The one endpoint\n\n`POST /api/audit` - Submit a URL, get back a full scored report.\n\n## Response shape\n\n```json\n{\n  \"url\": \"https://example.com\",\n  \"scannedAt\": \"2026-05-20T09:00:00Z\",\n  \"overallScore\": 72,\n  \"categories\": {\n    \"performance\": { \"score\": 65, \"checks\": [...] },\n    \"seo\":         { \"score\": 90, \"checks\": [...] },\n    \"trust\":       { \"score\": 75, \"checks\": [...] },\n    \"ux\":          { \"score\": 70, \"checks\": [...] },\n    \"mobile\":      { \"score\": 80, \"checks\": [...] },\n    \"accessibility\": { \"score\": 55, \"checks\": [...] }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Check status values\n- `pass` - all good\n- `warning` - needs attention\n- `fail` - significant issue\n\n## Score bands\n- 80-100 - Good (green)\n- 50-79 - Needs work (amber)\n- 0-49 - Poor (red)",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "base_url",
      "value": "http://localhost:3000",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Happy Path",
      "description": "Successful audit requests against real URLs.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Audit - webbeet.studio",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Has url field', () => pm.expect(json).to.have.property('url'));",
                  "pm.test('Has scannedAt field', () => pm.expect(json).to.have.property('scannedAt'));",
                  "pm.test('overallScore is a number 0-100', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(json.overallScore).to.be.a('number');",
                  "  pm.expect(json.overallScore).to.be.within(0, 100);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Has all 6 categories', () => {",
                  "  const cats = Object.keys(json.categories);",
                  "  ['performance','seo','trust','ux','mobile','accessibility'].forEach(c => {",
                  "    pm.expect(cats).to.include(c);",
                  "  });",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Each category has score and checks', () => {",
                  "  Object.values(json.categories).forEach(cat => {",
                  "    pm.expect(cat).to.have.property('score');",
                  "    pm.expect(cat).to.have.property('checks');",
                  "  });",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Each check has required fields', () => {",
                  "  Object.values(json.categories).forEach(cat => {",
                  "    cat.checks.forEach(check => {",
                  "      pm.expect(check).to.have.property('id');",
                  "      pm.expect(check).to.have.property('label');",
                  "      pm.expect(check).to.have.property('value');",
                  "      pm.expect(check).to.have.property('status');",
                  "      pm.expect(check).to.have.property('description');",
                  "      pm.expect(['pass','warning','fail']).to.include(check.status);",
                  "    });",
                  "  });",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "// Log scores for quick review",
                  "console.log('Overall:', json.overallScore);",
                  "Object.entries(json.categories).forEach(([k,v]) => {",
                  "  const flag = v.unavailable ? '(unavailable)' : '';",
                  "  console.log(` ${k}: ${v.score} ${flag}`);",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n    \"url\": \"https://webbeet.studio\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/audit",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["api", "audit"]
            },
            "description": "Full audit of webbeet.studio - the Webbeet homepage. Useful as a baseline benchmark."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Audit - example.com (fast, minimal)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('example.com should score well', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(json.overallScore).to.be.above(70);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Not timed out', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(json.timedOut).to.be.undefined;",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n    \"url\": \"https://example.com\"\n}",
